QA round 8 reasoning, for the next loop:

- The body-drain fix is deliberately central rather than per-branch: every earlier
  attempt at 'this branch also needs to read the body' regressed as soon as a new
  route was added. _route now owns framing, handlers only see self.body. If you add
  a route, you get the behaviour for free; if you read self.rfile again, you break it.
- Chunked bodies are refused (413 + close) rather than decoded. The gateway sits
  behind Caddy, which normalises to Content-Length, and a hand-rolled chunk parser is
  exactly the kind of code that desynchronises connections.
- The .synced marker lives inside the uv cache dir, so 'rm' takes it with the state
  dir and a re-apply resolves again. It is written 0600 and owned by root like the
  rest of the state dir; the unit only needs to read the cache, not the marker.
- remove_group_member uses gpasswd --delete, not usermod --groups: usermod rewrites
  the entire supplementary list, which would silently drop memberships smallapp does
  not know about. It is a no-op when the membership is already gone, so apply stays
  retryable.
- Criterion 26: the old test would have crashed, not passed, on Linux — the skip hid
  a bug in the test itself. Worth remembering that a permanently-skipped test is
  untested code. The docker fallback pulls debian:bookworm-slim and apt-installs
  systemd (~60s), which is why the test is marked slow. Recorded scores: both units
  0.9 SAFE against the 4.0 limit, systemd 252.
